### API Testing (VS Code “REST Client” extension, or copy to Postman)
@host = http://localhost:5000/api

### 0. Health
GET {{host}}/health

### 1. Registration
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ “name”: “Ana”, “email”: “ana@test.com”, ‘password’: “123456” }

### 2. Login (copy the token from the response)
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ “email”: “ana@test.com”, ‘password’: “123456” }

### 3. Profile
@token = PASTE_THE_TOKEN_HERE
GET {{host}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Create a playlist (CREATE)
POST {{host}}/playlists
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ “name”: “My first playlist”, “description”: ‘Test’, “isPublic”: false }

### 5. List my playlists (READ)
GET {{host}}/playlists
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. Edit playlist (UPDATE)  -> change ID
PUT {{host}}/playlists/PLAYLIST_ID
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ “name”: “New Name” }

### 7. Add a song
POST {{host}}/playlists/PLAYLIST_ID/tracks
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{ “youtubeId”: “dQw4w9WgXcQ”, “title”: “Test Song”, ‘channel’: “Channel” }

### 8. Delete playlist (DELETE)
DELETE {{host}}/playlists/PLAYLIST_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Authorization: A regular user should receive a 403 error
GET {{host}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Authorization: The admin can list users (admin token)
# GET {{host}}/users   with the token from admin@zelit.com

### 11. Without a token, it should return a 401
GET {{host}}/playlists

